==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|netze}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|nezzi}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*natją}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*ned-||to turn, twist, knot}}. Akin to Dutch {{m|nl|net}}, Low German {{m|nds|Nett}}, English {{m|en|net}}, Danish {{m|da|net}}, Swedish {{m|sv|nät}}.

